.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-ORBSTACK-TUNE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-orbstack-tune
.Nd raise the OrbStack VM memory limit
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad orbstack-tune
.Op Ar gb
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
raises the memory limit of the OrbStack virtual machine so the NOMAD stack has
more RAM to work with.
It requires the
.Ic orb
CLI, which ships with OrbStack.
.Pp
With no argument the target is 80% of host RAM, scaled to the machine, with at
least 4 GB reserved for macOS and a 4 GB floor for the VM.
An optional whole-number argument sets the target in GB explicitly.
.Pp
If OrbStack already allocates at least the target,
.Nm
makes no change.
Otherwise it asks for confirmation, then sets the limit and restarts OrbStack
to apply it, which briefly interrupts running containers.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar gb
Target memory in whole GB.
Overrides the default 80%-of-host calculation.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad orbstack-tune
Bump the VM to 80% of host RAM.
.It Ic nomad orbstack-tune 64
Set the VM memory limit to 64 GB.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-system 1
